R.I. Bagnall wrote:
> In article <4lf4tp$i8n@news.service.uci.edu>,
> I have a different problem with tcsh:
> I'm running v 6.04 and every time I log out I get a file dumped in the CWD
> called gmon.out. Its 21xxxx bytes in size (not always the same size).

Someone built your tcsh for call graph profiling with -pg.  Every time such
a program exits, it writes a gmon.out file so that you can analyze the gathered
statistics.  Read the gprof(1) man page for details.

Rebuild tcsh without -pg and it will work as you expect.
