DEC sells this compiler unbundled from the debugger and language 
development (i.e. class browser) tools, and usually doesn't bother to
tell you so until after you buy the compiler. The regular debugger that
you get with cxx is a c debugger that does not understand classes. So
you have to order the DECLA debugger. The preceding verbiage means that
at the end of the day you have to fork over US$4000 - US$5000 to get
a single usable c++ development environment on the alpha.

