    Rich> In <w5w91ffyu6m.fsf@mantis.austin.ibm.com> cc@austin.ibm.com writes:
    >> Can you identify the principals in these cases, particularly for secd?
    >> - I know there's dce-rgy, what are the other two?
    Rich> dce-ptgt.  And one for the AS but I forget what.

    >> Also, a while back I posted a question about what happens when two 
    >> key management threads run against the same principal/keytab entry?
    >> Is this safe?  

    Rich> Probably not.  Why would you want to do this?
