It's not that I want, but that I want to know if I have to protect
against it.  I wrote a wrapper to authenticate to dce, fork and exec a
long-running process (non-dce) and then start a context refresher and
key management thread in the parent.

Unfortunately, it occurred to me that someone might get lazy and try
to use the "self" principal or another key managed locally by dced.
Is there any easy way to detect "management" of a key?   (A simple
fix would be to try to lock the KeyFile to prevent a second process
from doing anything!)

  
