Ravi Bahethi <bahethi@grid.gsfc.nasa.gov> wrote:
>Hello,
>
>	Has anyone installed Ghostscript on a Alpha running 
>Digital Unix (OSF). If so, what changes were made to the makefile?
>
>you help is greatly appreciated.
>
>Thanks
>Ravi Bahethi
>

I installed ghostscript-3.51 with fonts-3.0 (std + other) on DU3.2C
(compiled with gcc-2.7.2)

Just read carefully the file "make.doc". The makefile was just modified
with "installbsd" instead of "install"
Before compiling, you'll need to have jpeg sources in the gs directory :

cd gs351
gzcat jpegsrc.v6.tar.gz |tar xvf -

and then all is fine.

The fonts have to be installed in /usr/local/lib/ghostscript/fonts (NOT in
the directory told in "make.doc", they are not found).

Let me know if you have other problems.

