Who should attend

Technical professionals who require an in-depth knowledge of the OSF's
Distributed Computing Environment. This course should be attended by
software engineers, programmers and system architects who are proficient 
in C and who have a good basic understanding of DCE.

Course Summary

This new OSF DCE Internals Architecture course provides detailed
architectural coverage of the components of DCE 1.1 and how they 
comprise an integrated approach to distributed computing. The DCE 
Internals course is a lecture-based curriculum covering key principles 
and topics, and reinforced by diagrams and examples. Having attended 
this course the engineer/programmer will be able to describe the 
components of DCE at internals level detail and how they work with one 
another to provide full DCE functionality. Students will also gain an 
understanding of the implementation of the components of DCE and their 
interaction with operating system services.

